From cfb3d22d9cb5562d544eaf9ac7c9fd10babfc111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Wu <Henry_Wu@quantatw.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:49:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] requester: complete queued requests on endpoint cancellation

Endpoint request queues can be left with waiters when an
endpoint is removed while requests are active or pending.
Add endpoint-wide cancellation that stops active requests,
frees instance IDs, drains queued requests, and completes
waiters with an empty response so coroutines follow the
existing timeout/error path.

Also complete a dequeued request when starting the transport
request or its expiry timer fails. This lets the endpoint
queue continue polling instead of leaving the coroutine
suspended forever.

Add coverage for the dequeued send-failure path.

The link of upstream:
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/95349

Change-Id: I3f6e4d38b623b402871b83064ec057e524088add
Signed-off-by: Henry Wu <Henry_Wu@quantatw.com>
